## Receiving Imagine (2026-11-27)

Disposition: accept findings1/2 only for documentation implementation in
child1573. Other findings are held for author decisions or already covered,
as the table records. The author's instruction authorizes a raid on accepted
scope; the pilot-specific panel signature remains a deviation, not general
authority. This tracker stays open.

1. **Facts against framing.** Read RESULTS.md, PROTOCOL.md, both comparison
   reports, and the relevant DEVIATIONS sections at replicator df890ef. They
   report two frozen case runs and post-freeze comparisons, not an accuracy
   estimate or an independently established general benefit from panel signing.
   Atanasov's comparison records missed merge/construction problems and a
   borderline pass assessment. This reception did not rerun estimates, verify
   every freeze hash, or independently certify the blindness audits.
2. **Duplicates and overlap.** Read current SKILL.md, assessment.md and rules.md
   after1568/1569/1571. Current probe already records anomalies as candidates,
   every planned disposition, and renewed signature for amendments. Report
   already prints all six rows with explicit unresolved statuses, and rule2
   already requires three digits. Rebuild/lock the authors' environment is
   already required. The audit of joins and construction definitions remains
   an operational gap; it is the sole accepted implementation child.
3. **Ownership and placement.** Harness owns generic reproduction audit
   guidance under SKILL.md reproduce and its evidence requirements. Replicator
   owns numerical reruns, paper-specific corrections, container images and
   report repairs. Keep package files immutable. Audit the authors' actual
   keys before normalization; corrections remain separate and labelled. A
   text/code discrepancy enters an anomaly ledger, not an automatic coding
   error: the Atanasov Table3 note conflicts with otherwise agreeing text/code.
4. **Standing rulings and fit.** Preserve person-written signatures, the
   printed-digit comparison tolerance, canonical ACRe/whole-paper meanings,
   author control over robustness specifications, and route's consent rules.
   Different-family review is sought with authorized routes and unavailable
   perspectives disclosed; no implicit paid spending is granted. The pilot
   report is now available for1570, but general signing authority still needs
   an author ruling. Two cases cannot settle that ruling or rescore old runs.

